    <section class="slide" data-title="Research questions and hypotheses" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Research questions and hypotheses</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Research questions and hypotheses</h2>
          <div class="compare-table">
            <article><h3>Qualitative research</h3><ul><li>Uses research questions</li><li>Seeks information on a single concept</li><li>Asks participants to share ideas and builds general themes</li><li>Uses a more open-ended stance</li><li>Seeks a deep understanding of the views of one group or single individuals</li></ul></article>
            <article><h3>Quantitative research</h3><ul><li>Uses hypotheses</li><li>Identifies and measures multiple variables</li><li>Tests theories that predict results from relating variables</li><li>Uses a closed-ended stance and selects instruments before the study begins</li><li>Measures differences among groups or changes over time</li></ul></article>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>研究問題與假設</h2>
          <div class="compare-table">
            <article><h3>定性研究</h3><ul><li>使用研究問題</li><li>尋求有關單一概念的資料</li><li>請參與者分享想法，並建立一般主題</li><li>採用較開放的立場</li><li>深入理解一個群體或個別人士的觀點</li></ul></article>
            <article><h3>定量研究</h3><ul><li>使用假設</li><li>識別並測量多個變量</li><li>檢驗從變量關係預測結果的理論</li><li>採用封閉式立場，並在研究開始前選擇工具</li><li>測量群體差異或個體隨時間的變化</li></ul></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Hypothesis" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Hypothesis</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Hypothesis</h2>
          <p class="lead medium">Hypotheses are statements in quantitative research in which the investigator makes a prediction or conjecture about the outcome of a relationship among attributes or characteristics.</p>
          <p class="lead medium">These predictions are not simply an “educated guess”. Hypotheses are made because past studies in the literature suggest certain outcomes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>假設</h2>
          <p class="lead medium">假設是定量研究中的陳述，研究者對屬性或特徵之間關係的結果作出預測或推測。</p>
          <p class="lead medium">這些預測並不只是「有根據的猜測」。提出假設，是因為過往文獻研究顯示某些結果。</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Null and alternative hypotheses" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">The null and alternative hypotheses</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Null and alternative hypotheses</h2>
          <div class="hypothesis-pair">
            <article><h3>Null hypothesis H₀</h3><p>Tests in the general population that there is no change, no relationship or no difference.</p><p class="formula">There is no difference (or relationship) between…</p></article>
            <article><h3>Alternative hypothesis H₁, H₂, H₃…</h3><p>May be true if the null is rejected; suggests a change, relationship or difference.</p><p class="formula">Higher · lower · more positive · more favourable</p></article>
          </div>
          <h3 class="hypothesis-subtitle">Directional and non-directional</h3>
          <div class="hypothesis-pair hypothesis-followup">
            <article><h3>Directional alternative hypothesis</h3><p>Students who participate in direct learning in four elementary schools will have <strong>higher</strong> achievement scores than students who participate in whole-language learning.</p></article>
            <article><h3>Non-directional alternative hypothesis</h3><p>There is <strong>a difference</strong> between varsity athletes in high school who smoke and those who do not smoke in terms of athletic accomplishments.</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>零假設與備擇假設</h2>
          <div class="hypothesis-pair">
            <article><h3>零假設 H₀</h3><p>在一般母體中檢驗沒有變化、沒有關係或沒有差異。</p><p class="formula">……之間沒有差異（或關係）</p></article>
            <article><h3>備擇假設 H₁、H₂、H₃……</h3><p>若零假設被拒絕，則可能成立；表示有變化、關係或差異。</p><p class="formula">較高 · 較低 · 更正面 · 更有利</p></article>
          </div>
          <h3 class="hypothesis-subtitle">方向性與非方向性</h3>
          <div class="hypothesis-pair hypothesis-followup">
            <article><h3>方向性備擇假設</h3><p>四所小學中參加直接教學的學生，成就分數將<strong>高於</strong>參加全語言教學的學生。</p></article>
            <article><h3>非方向性備擇假設</h3><p>高中校隊運動員中吸煙者與不吸煙者的運動成就<strong>存在差異</strong>。</p></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Tips for hypotheses" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Tips for hypotheses</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Tips for hypotheses</h2>
          <ul class="source-list">
            <li><strong>State variables clearly:</strong> independent variable first, dependent variable second, control variables third.</li>
            <li><strong>If comparing groups:</strong> explicitly state which groups are compared.</li>
            <li><strong>If testing relationships:</strong> specify the type of relationship: positive, negative or no relationship.</li>
            <li>These predictions are tested statistically.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>假設的提示</h2>
          <ul class="source-list">
            <li><strong>清楚說明變量：</strong>先自變量，其次因變量，再次控制變量。</li>
            <li><strong>若比較群體：</strong>明確說明比較哪些群體。</li>
            <li><strong>若檢驗關係：</strong>說明關係類型：正向、負向或沒有關係。</li>
            <li>這些預測會以統計方法進行檢驗。</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Concept, construct and variable" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">From ideas to measurement</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Concept, construct and variable</h2>
          <div class="concept-grid">
            <details class="concept-card"><summary><span class="concept-step">01</span><span>Concept</span></summary><div class="concept-card-body"><p>A generalisable property or characteristic associated with an object, event or person.</p><p class="example-line">A student is an object of study; the student’s motivation is a concept.</p></div></details>
            <details class="concept-card"><summary><span class="concept-step">02</span><span>Construct</span></summary><div class="concept-card-body"><p>An abstract concept chosen or created to explain a phenomenon. It may combine several related concepts.</p><p class="example-line">Communication skill may include vocabulary, syntax and spelling.</p></div></details>
            <details class="concept-card"><summary><span class="concept-step">03</span><span>Variable</span></summary><div class="concept-card-body"><p>A measurable representation, or proxy, of a construct. Its value can vary across the cases studied.</p><p class="example-line">Intelligence is a construct; IQ score is a variable used to measure it.</p></div></details>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>概念、構念與變量</h2>
          <div class="concept-grid">
            <details class="concept-card"><summary><span class="concept-step">01</span><span>概念</span></summary><div class="concept-card-body"><p>與物件、事件或人物相關，而且可以概括的屬性或特徵。</p><p class="example-line">學生是研究對象；學生的動機是一個概念。</p></div></details>
            <details class="concept-card"><summary><span class="concept-step">02</span><span>構念</span></summary><div class="concept-card-body"><p>為解釋某種現象而選擇或創建的抽象概念，可以由幾個相關概念組成。</p><p class="example-line">溝通能力可以包括詞彙、句法和拼寫。</p></div></details>
            <details class="concept-card"><summary><span class="concept-step">03</span><span>變量</span></summary><div class="concept-card-body"><p>構念的可測量表徵或代理指標，其數值可以因研究個案而異。</p><p class="example-line">智力是構念；智商分數是用來測量它的變量。</p></div></details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide concept-measure-slide" data-title="From construct to variable" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">From ideas to measurement</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Move from abstract to measurable</h2>
          <div class="illustration-layout">
            <figure>
              <div class="research-plane-diagram" role="img" aria-label="Construct A and Construct B connected by a proposition on the theoretical plane, with corresponding independent and dependent variables connected by a hypothesis on the empirical plane.">
                <div class="diagram-plane theoretical-plane"><span class="plane-label">Theoretical plane</span><span class="diagram-node">Construct A</span><span class="diagram-relation"><b>→</b><small>Proposition</small></span><span class="diagram-node">Construct B</span></div>
                <div class="operational-links" aria-hidden="true"><span>↓</span><small>Operationalise</small><span>↓</span></div>
                <div class="diagram-plane empirical-plane"><span class="plane-label">Empirical plane</span><span class="diagram-node">Independent variable</span><span class="diagram-relation"><b>→</b><small>Hypothesis</small></span><span class="diagram-node">Dependent variable</span></div>
              </div>
              <figcaption>Constructs become measurable variables through operational definitions.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <ol class="illustration-notes">
              <li><strong>Theoretical plane:</strong> constructs are abstract ideas connected by propositions.</li>
              <li><strong>Operational bridge:</strong> define exactly how each construct will be measured.</li>
              <li><strong>Empirical plane:</strong> variables contain the observed values tested in hypotheses.</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <div class="measure-examples">
            <p><strong>Intelligence</strong> <span>construct</span> → <strong>IQ score</strong> <span>variable</span></p>
            <p><strong>Academic achievement</strong> <span>construct</span> → <strong>GPA</strong> <span>variable</span></p>
          </div>
          <p class="measurement-check"><strong>Always ask:</strong> Does this variable represent the construct well?</p>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>從抽象概念走向測量</h2>
          <div class="illustration-layout">
            <figure>
              <div class="research-plane-diagram" role="img" aria-label="理論層面的構念 A 與構念 B 由命題連接，並透過自變量與因變量在經驗層面形成可檢驗的假設。">
                <div class="diagram-plane theoretical-plane"><span class="plane-label">理論層面</span><span class="diagram-node">構念 A</span><span class="diagram-relation"><b>→</b><small>命題</small></span><span class="diagram-node">構念 B</span></div>
                <div class="operational-links" aria-hidden="true"><span>↓</span><small>操作化</small><span>↓</span></div>
                <div class="diagram-plane empirical-plane"><span class="plane-label">經驗層面</span><span class="diagram-node">自變量</span><span class="diagram-relation"><b>→</b><small>假設</small></span><span class="diagram-node">因變量</span></div>
              </div>
              <figcaption>透過操作性定義，把構念轉化為可測量的變量。</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <ol class="illustration-notes">
              <li><strong>理論層面：</strong>構念是抽象想法，彼此由命題連接。</li>
              <li><strong>操作化橋樑：</strong>明確界定每個構念將如何測量。</li>
              <li><strong>經驗層面：</strong>變量包含觀察所得的數值，並用於檢驗假設。</li>
            </ol>
          </div>
          <div class="measure-examples">
            <p><strong>智力</strong> <span>構念</span> → <strong>智商分數</strong> <span>變量</span></p>
            <p><strong>學業成就</strong> <span>構念</span> → <strong>平均績點</strong> <span>變量</span></p>
          </div>
          <p class="measurement-check"><strong>始終要問：</strong>這個變量是否能良好地代表該構念？</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Activity 4: The family of variables" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">Activity 4: The family of variables</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>The family of variables</h2>
          <div class="variable-form">
            <label>What outcomes in my study am I trying to explain?<textarea data-save="outcomes"></textarea></label>
            <label>What variables or factors influence the outcomes?<textarea data-save="factors"></textarea></label>
            <label>What variables do I need to also measure (i.e., control) so that I can make sure that my major factors influence outcomes and not other factors?<textarea data-save="controls"></textarea></label>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>變量家族</h2>
          <div class="variable-form">
            <label>我的研究試圖解釋哪些結果？<textarea data-save="outcomes-zh"></textarea></label>
            <label>哪些變量或因素影響這些結果？<textarea data-save="factors-zh"></textarea></label>
            <label>我還需要測量哪些變量（即控制變量），以確保主要因素而不是其他因素影響結果？<textarea data-save="controls-zh"></textarea></label>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="Types of variables" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">The family of variables</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Types of variables</h2>
          <div class="variable-types">
            <details><summary>Control variable</summary><p>Extraneous variables whose influence can be controlled or eliminated. Example: gender, socioeconomic status, age or race.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Independent variable</summary><p>A construct considered to be the cause in a theoretical framework. Example: higher education leads to higher income.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Dependent variable</summary><p>A construct considered to be the effect in a theoretical framework. Example: aerobic exercise reduces state anxiety.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Intervening or mediating variable</summary><p>A construct that intervenes, mediates or stands between cause and effect.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Moderating variable</summary><p>Moderates the relationship between two variables.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Covariate</summary><p>A measured variable included to account for variation in the dependent variable.</p></details>
            <details><summary>Confounding or lurking variable</summary><p>A rival explanation for a cause-and-effect relationship. Example: age explains the relationship between shoe size and intelligence in children.</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>變量的類型</h2>
          <div class="variable-types">
            <details><summary>控制變量</summary><p>其影響可以被控制或消除的外來變量，例如性別、社會經濟地位、年齡或種族。</p></details>
            <details><summary>自變量</summary><p>在理論框架中被視為原因的構念，例如高等教育導致較高收入。</p></details>
            <details><summary>因變量</summary><p>在理論框架中被視為效果的構念，例如有氧運動降低狀態焦慮。</p></details>
            <details><summary>介入或中介變量</summary><p>介入、中介或處於原因與效果之間的構念。</p></details>
            <details><summary>調節變量</summary><p>調節兩個變量之間的關係。</p></details>
            <details><summary>協變量</summary><p>納入測量，以解釋因變量變異的變量。</p></details>
            <details><summary>混淆或潛伏變量</summary><p>因果關係的競爭解釋，例如年齡解釋兒童鞋碼與智力之間的關係。</p></details>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide" data-title="How variables work together" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">The family of variables</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>How variables work together</h2>
          <div class="variable-illustration">
            <figure>
              <div class="variable-model-diagram" role="img" aria-label="Intelligence as an independent variable influences academic achievement as a mediating variable, which influences earning potential as a dependent variable. Effort moderates the first relationship.">
                <span class="moderator-node"><small>Moderating variable</small><strong>Effort</strong><b aria-hidden="true">↓</b></span>
                <span class="model-node independent-node"><strong>Intelligence</strong><small>Independent variable</small></span>
                <span class="model-arrow first-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <span class="model-node mediator-node"><strong>Academic achievement</strong><small>Mediating variable</small></span>
                <span class="model-arrow second-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <span class="model-node dependent-node"><strong>Earning potential</strong><small>Dependent variable</small></span>
              </div>
              <figcaption>One model can assign different roles to its variables.</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <dl>
              <div><dt>Independent</dt><dd>Explains or predicts another variable.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Dependent</dt><dd>The outcome explained by another variable.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Mediating</dt><dd>Shows the mechanism through which an effect works.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Moderating</dt><dd>Strengthens, weakens or changes an effect.</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="zh" hidden lang="zh-Hant">
          <h2>變量如何共同作用</h2>
          <div class="variable-illustration">
            <figure>
              <div class="variable-model-diagram" role="img" aria-label="智力作為自變量影響學業成就這個中介變量，再影響賺取收入的潛力這個因變量；努力調節第一段關係。">
                <span class="moderator-node"><small>調節變量</small><strong>努力</strong><b aria-hidden="true">↓</b></span>
                <span class="model-node independent-node"><strong>智力</strong><small>自變量</small></span>
                <span class="model-arrow first-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <span class="model-node mediator-node"><strong>學業成就</strong><small>中介變量</small></span>
                <span class="model-arrow second-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
                <span class="model-node dependent-node"><strong>賺取收入的潛力</strong><small>因變量</small></span>
              </div>
              <figcaption>同一個模型可為不同變量指定不同角色。</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <dl>
              <div><dt>自變量</dt><dd>解釋或預測另一個變量。</dd></div>
              <div><dt>因變量</dt><dd>由另一個變量解釋的結果。</dd></div>
              <div><dt>中介變量</dt><dd>顯示某個效果透過甚麼機制發生。</dd></div>
              <div><dt>調節變量</dt><dd>增強、減弱或改變某個效果。</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="slide confounder-slide" data-title="Confounders and covariates" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="slide-inner">
        <header class="slide-header"><span class="eyebrow">The family of variables</span><button class="translate-button" type="button" aria-pressed="false">中文</button></header>
        <div class="language-panel" data-language="en">
          <h2>Confounders and covariates</h2>
          <div class="confounder-layout">
            <div class="variable-definition-pair">
              <article><h3>Confounder</h3><p>Influences both the independent and dependent variables. It can inflate or deflate their apparent relationship and affect internal validity.</p></article>
              <article><h3>Covariate</h3><p>Influences the dependent variable and has little or no relationship with the other variables in the model.</p></article>
            </div>
            <figure>
              <div class="confounder-map" role="img" aria-label="A covariate points to the dependent variable, the independent variable points to the dependent variable, and a confounder points to both the independent and dependent variables.">
                <span class="map-node covariate-map-node">Covariate</span><span class="map-arrow covariate-map-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↘</span>
                <span class="map-node iv-map-node">Independent variable</span><span class="map-arrow iv-map-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span class="map-node dv-map-node">Dependent variable</span>
